  <section id="rules" class="dashboard-panel">
    <h2>Lockdown game rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Respect other players.</strong> Keep rivalry inside the game. No threats, harassment, hate speech or sharing someone else's private information.</li>
      <li><strong>Play fairly.</strong> Do not use cheats, bots, scripts or exploits to gain an unfair advantage. Report a bug to the game owner instead of abusing it.</li>
      <li><strong>Protect accounts.</strong> Use your own account, keep your password private and never ask another player for their login details.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep communication useful.</strong> Do not spam the Shoutbox, send abusive messages or impersonate another player or a member of staff.</li>
      <li><strong>Trade honestly.</strong> Check the item, quantity and total asking price before buying or listing. Do not misrepresent an item or arrange trades using stolen accounts.</li>
      <li><strong>Accept in-game consequences.</strong> Crimes can land you in jail; battles can cost health and money. Read costs, requirements and recovery timers before committing to an action.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Need help? Ask in the <a href="/shoutbox">Shoutbox</a>. Use <a href="/mail">Mail</a> for a private conversation, and contact the game owner about account problems or suspected cheating. Never post your password.</p>
  </section>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="getting-started" open>
    <summary><h2>1. Getting started</h2><span>Home, training, work and education</span></summary>
    <p>Before chasing the big money, get familiar with your character and build a routine.</p>
    <h3>Visit your home overview</h3>
    <ol><li>Click <a href="/home">Home</a> at the top or in the left menu.</li><li>Check your cash, level, reputation and daily objectives. Your header shows health, energy, nerve, happiness, stamina and experience.</li><li>Open <a href="/account">My Account</a> for more personal details or <a href="/property">My Property</a> to manage your home.</li></ol>
    <h3>Increase your stats</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/gym">The Gym</a>.</li><li>Choose a whole number of energy points to spend. Start with 1 if you are learning.</li><li>Click Train on Strength, Defense, Speed or Dexterity. Each energy point uses 2% stamina and 1 happiness; you need enough energy and stamina to train.</li></ol>
    <h3>Get your first job</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/jobs">Job Listings</a> from the left menu.</li><li>Compare the defense requirement, daily pay and XP. Choose an eligible job and click Take Job.</li><li>Your pay arrives automatically when due, with an event notification. Return here to see your current job and next payment.</li></ol>
    <h3>Start an education course</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/education">Education</a> and read each course's cost, duration and permanent perk.</li><li>Choose an available course and click Enroll. You pay cash; enrollment does not cost energy or nerve.</li><li>Study continues offline. When the timer finishes, return and click Collect perk to activate it. Finish and collect your current course before starting another.</li></ol>
    <p class="guide-tip">Your first goal: one training session, a job and a course you can afford. Getting established is more useful than spending all your cash at once.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="first-fight">
    <summary><h2>2. Prepare for your first fight</h2><span>Buy a melee weapon and equip it</span></summary>
    <p>Good preparation makes a bigger difference than picking the first opponent you see.</p>
    <h3>Buy a melee weapon</h3>
    <ol><li>Open the <a href="/market">Marketplace</a> and select Melee.</li><li>Compare prices and the Lockdown effect shown on each item. Choose an in-stock weapon, set the quantity to 1 and click Buy. Stock is shared and rotates hourly; sold-out items must wait for restocking.</li><li>Open <a href="/inventory">My Inventory</a>, find your weapon and click Equip. Check the equipped loadout to confirm it is ready.</li></ol>
    <h3>Choose an opponent carefully</h3>
    <ol><li>Visit <a href="/battles">Battles</a> to see eligible citizens in your city. You can also browse <a href="/citizens">Citizens</a> and open their profiles.</li><li>Compare the displayed stats. Equipment and property bonuses can make an opponent stronger than the listed base stats.</li><li>Train first if you are not ready. Battles are against other players, so there is no guaranteed easy practice target.</li></ol>
    <h3>Fight and review the result</h3>
    <ol><li>On Battles, choose a stance and your preferred victory outcome. Leave gives extra XP and reputation when you win.</li><li>You need 5 energy and at least 10% stamina to attack. You must be in the same city and free of jail or hospital restrictions.</li><li>Click Attack and read the battle report. The fight resolves automatically using your stats and equipped items.</li><li>Afterward, check your health and resources. Train again only if you have enough energy and stamina.</li></ol>
    <p class="guide-tip">One weapon, one armor item and one gear item can be equipped at a time. Buying something alone does not equip it.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="exploring-one">
    <summary><h2>3. Exploring the city, part one</h2><span>Shops, property, trading and meeting people</span></summary>
    <h3>Learn your way around</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/city">City</a> to explore the map. Select a location pin or switch to Quick Links to visit a service. There is a 35% chance of a random item appearing each UTC day; click the item on the map to add it to Items. Refreshing does not change your daily result, and each find can only be collected once.</li><li>Visit <a href="/market">Marketplace</a> for the shop catalog. Search by name, filter by category and sort by price.</li><li>Visit <a href="/openmarket">Open Market</a> for items listed by other players. Read the quantity and total asking price before buying.</li><li>Open <a href="/property">My Property</a> and <a href="/broker-supplies">the property store</a> to see furnishings and upgrades. Check a furnishing's bonuses before spending.</li><li>Visit the <a href="/shoutbox">Shoutbox</a> to introduce yourself or ask a question. Use <a href="/mail">Mail</a> to talk privately.</li></ol>
    <h3>Turn spare items into cash</h3>
    <ol><li>Open My Inventory and find a tradeable item you own.</li><li>Click Sell, enter the quantity and set the <strong>total</strong> asking price for the listing.</li><li>After another player buys it, you receive 90% of the sale price. The remaining 10% is the market fee.</li></ol>
    <p class="guide-tip">Keep items you need for your next goal. A low purchase price does not guarantee a profitable resale.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="criminal-methods">
    <summary><h2>4. Criminal methods</h2><span>Earn cash, manage heat and build experience</span></summary>
    <p>The streets offer opportunities, but every attempt has a cost and a chance of getting caught.</p>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/crimes">Commit Crimes</a> and browse the crimes available in your city.</li><li>Read the nerve cost, stamina cost, payout and catch risk. Start with a lower-risk option you can afford.</li><li>Choose Cautious, Balanced or Bold. Cautious reduces risk and reward; Bold raises both.</li><li>Commit the crime and read the result. Success earns cash, XP, reputation and criminal experience. Getting caught sends you to jail.</li><li>Watch your heat. Higher heat raises risk, and it cools down over time. Repeating successful crimes builds mastery, improving their risk and rewards.</li><li>Save toward your first $250 earned from crimes, then review whether to invest in training, supplies or education.</li></ol>
    <p>Successful crimes also build nerve capacity over time. Available crimes depend on your home city; use the options and costs shown on your own crime page.</p>
    <p class="guide-tip">Do not spend the last of your cash assuming the next crime will succeed. Keep a reserve for supplies and recovery.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="weapons">
    <summary><h2>5. Weapons, equipment &amp; other players</h2><span>Upgrade your loadout and understand combat</span></summary>
    <h3>Buy and equip a gun</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/market">Marketplace</a> and browse Primary or Secondary weapons.</li><li>Check the price, availability and Lockdown stat bonuses, then buy a weapon you can afford.</li><li>Go to <a href="/inventory">My Inventory</a> and click Equip. A gun replaces the weapon in your single weapon slot.</li></ol>
    <p>Your equipped weapon contributes its bonuses automatically in battle. There is no separate ammo purchase or reload step.</p>
    <h3>Choose your fight plan</h3>
    <ul><li><strong>Balanced:</strong> standard attack and defense.</li><li><strong>Aggressive:</strong> more attack power at the cost of defense.</li><li><strong>Defensive:</strong> more protection at the cost of attack power.</li><li><strong>Leave:</strong> more XP and reputation on victory.</li><li><strong>Mug:</strong> steal a portion of the defeated player's cash on hand, with less XP.</li><li><strong>Hospitalize:</strong> keep a defeated rival in recovery longer.</li></ul>
    <p>Choose the outcome before clicking Attack on <a href="/battles">Battles</a>. Check the combat log afterward. A 10-minute cooldown applies before attacking the same player again.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="exploring-two">
    <summary><h2>6. Exploring the city, part two</h2><span>Hospital, jail, bank and factions</span></summary>
    <h3>Know where to recover</h3>
    <ul><li><a href="/hospital">Hospital:</a> check recovery time and the available treatment options. Defeat can put you here. Review any treatment price before paying.</li><li><a href="/jail">City Jail:</a> check your sentence and available release options. Training and crimes are restricted while you are locked up.</li><li><a href="/inventory">My Inventory:</a> usable supplies show a Use button and recovery timer. Read their Lockdown effect before using them; collection items have no direct use effect.</li></ul>
    <h3>Manage your money</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/bank">My Bank Account</a>.</li><li>Enter a whole amount to deposit or withdraw and confirm the resulting balance.</li><li>Keep enough cash on hand for your plans. Banked cash is not taken by an ordinary mugging..</li></ol>
    <h3>Meet a faction</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/factions">Known Factions</a> and read about the groups in the city.</li><li>Talk to members before committing. Check <a href="/faction-invites">Faction Invites</a> if someone invites you.</li><li>After joining, use <a href="/my-faction">My Faction</a> to see the group and its available actions. Follow your faction's expectations and the game rules.</li></ol>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="stats">
    <summary><h2>7. Effective stat building</h2><span>Build all four battle stats</span></summary>
    <p>A strong fighter needs more than a hard punch. Open <a href="/gym">The Gym</a> and work toward these beginner targets:</p>
    <ol><li><strong>Strength to 12:</strong> improves the damage you deal.</li><li><strong>Dexterity to 12:</strong> helps you evade incoming attacks.</li><li><strong>Speed to 12:</strong> improves your chance to hit and helps determine who attacks first.</li><li><strong>Defense to 12:</strong> reduces the damage you take.</li><li><strong>Any stat to 15:</strong> choose the next improvement that suits your fighting style, then keep developing the others.</li></ol>
    <p>These are suggested training goals. Training history lets you follow your progress. Spending energy at the gym unlocks better gyms, while collected education perks can improve your gains.</p>
    <p>Happiness above 100 improves training gains, up to 25%. Distinct furnishings placed in your property raise your happiness cap, up to 200. Happiness recovers over time, and a home break on the overview can restore some for cash when available.</p>
    <p class="guide-tip">Train in sessions you can afford. If stamina is low, use less energy and return after recovery.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="exploring-three">
    <summary><h2>8. Exploring the city, part three</h2><span>Daily objectives, reputation and travel</span></summary>
    <h3>Complete your daily objectives</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/home#daily">Daily Objectives</a> on the overview.</li><li>Make 3 crime attempts and complete 2 training sessions during the current UTC day.</li><li>Return to claim the displayed reward: $500 and 3 reputation. You can claim it once per day; the objectives reset at midnight UTC.</li></ol>
    <h3>Follow your progress</h3>
    <p>Use <a href="/most-wanted">Most Wanted</a> to see how citizens rank by reputation. Check your overview, profile and <a href="/events">Events</a> for progress and updates.</p>
    <h3>Take a trading trip</h3>
    <ol><li>Open the <a href="/airport">Airport</a> to review trip costs, travel times and cargo. Read the destination's offers before departing.</li><li>Return home to resume local actions such as training, crimes and banking. Manage your trip and cargo on the Airport page.</li><li>Each country has 12 fixed shop items with shared hourly restocks. Boosters and caches appear rarely and expire after 20 minutes. Compare overseas prices with home prices before buying.</li></ol>
    <p class="guide-tip">Your home, job and bank stay in place while you travel. Cargo arrives in your inventory after your return flight. Sell imports to other players through the Open Market.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="dashboard-panel guide-chapter" id="next-steps">
    <summary><h2>9. Well on your way</h2><span>Better protection, a better home and level two</span></summary>
    <h3>Buy armor and gear</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/market">Marketplace</a> and choose Armor. Compare the defense and other bonuses, then buy an available item.</li><li>Visit <a href="/inventory">My Inventory</a> and equip it. Add gear when you can afford a useful upgrade.</li><li>Check your loadout: one weapon, one armor item and one gear item. Switching equipment changes your bonuses.</li></ol>
    <h3>Improve your property</h3>
    <ol><li>Open <a href="/property">My Property</a> and inspect the space and bonuses you already have.</li><li>Browse the properties on My Property, buy one you can afford and click Move in. Use the furnishing store below to buy things for your home.</li><li>Click Add to home beside a stored furnishing to activate its benefits. Items left in storage are not placed furnishings.</li></ol>
    <h3>Reach level two</h3>
    <p>Earn XP through training, successful crimes, work and battles. Qualifying actions level you up automatically when you have enough XP. Watch your level and experience bar; you do not need a separate upgrade button.</p>
    <h3>Build a daily routine</h3>
    <p>Train, work toward daily objectives, keep a course running and collect it when ready. Review Events and Mail, manage spare items and save for your next upgrade. Your next milestone might be a better gym, a new course, higher reputation or another city.</p>
    <p class="guide-tip">You have learned the basics. Keep a reserve, choose your battles and take breaks when resources are low. Progress comes from returning with a plan.</p>
  </details>

  <section class="dashboard-panel" id="resources">
    <h2>Resource quick reference</h2>
    <dl class="guide-resources">
      <dt>Health (HP)</dt><dd>Your ability to survive a fight. Check the Hospital or usable medical supplies when hurt.</dd>
      <dt>Energy (NRG)</dt><dd>Used for training and attacks. Recovers by 1 every 5 minutes, up to your cap.</dd>
      <dt>Nerve (NRV)</dt><dd>Used for crimes. Recovers by 1 every 3 minutes, up to your cap.</dd>
      <dt>Happiness (HAP)</dt><dd>Helps gym gains above 100. Recovers by 5 every 15 minutes, up to your cap.</dd>
      <dt>Stamina (STM)</dt><dd>Used for training, crimes and fighting. Recovers by 1% every 5 minutes, up to 100%.</dd>
      <dt>Experience (EXP)</dt><dd>Builds toward your next level. Reputation is a separate measure of your standing in the city.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>Recovery continues while you are offline. Supplies have shared cooldowns: using one can delay another in the same recovery group. Read the effect and timer shown in My Inventory.</p>
    <p>Guide chapters are a walkthrough to follow yourself. They do not award mission credits or automatic chapter rewards. Daily objectives and individual activities show the rewards you can earn.</p>
